    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #261\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully.\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-103-inbox-pipeline-03-07-dispatch-deduplic-thr_bj2aaphg93`\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #103: dispatches deduplicated Inbox item events.\n\n- Registers three `onItemEvent` heartbeats on the Inbox database (create/update/delete), each dispatching a new `semprec.tick` action.\n- Reuses the existing `triggerOnItemEventHeartbeats`/`heartbeatFireJobKey` machinery (already wired into the generic choke-point create/update/delete paths), so each event type gets its own heartbeat row and thus its own job key — different items and different event kinds never collide, and `job_key_mode: \"replace\"` collapses rapid repeat edits to the same item into a single pending job.\n- The `semprec.tick` handler (`inbox/inboxTickAction.ts`) re-reads the item by id at run time rather than trusting the job payload, so a collapsed job always reflects current state. Actual fingerprinting/proposal computation is out of scope (issue #223).\n- Added a small \"queue affinity\" concept (action id → graphile-worker `queue_name`), threaded through the choke point's create/update/delete paths, so `semprec.tick` (or any future action) can request serialized execution.\n- New test file `inboxTick.test.ts` covers: heartbeat registration, transactional per-event enqueue, cross-event/cross-item non-collision, rapid-update collapsing with latest-state reads, rollback emitting no job, and queue-affinity routing.\n\nFull test suite: 18 files / 247 tests, all passing.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
